Build:

docker build -t updater-image .


Run while mounting Dockersocket:

docker run --rm -it -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock -p 9090:9090 updater-image


(By default, updater.py will pull and start nginx:latest. can change when working properly)


Specifying a Custom Image:
If you want the updater to pull and start a different image, set the IMAGE_NAME environment variable, meaning replace nginx:latest in this example:

curl -X PUT -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"image_name": "nginx:latest"}' http://localhost:9090/update-image


Another container can invoke this updater container simply by running the docker run command above with the appropriate IMAGE_NAME environment variable set.



